From: Zurker <91011862+hershate@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:54:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Papo: batch 143 (R5) release the per-chunk NoiseChunk after
 the carvers step - the only readers of ChunkAccess.noiseChunk are the
 BIOMES/NOISE/SURFACE/CARVERS generation steps (NoiseBasedChunkGenerator via
 getOrCreateNoiseChunk); chunks parked between carvers and FULL (the
 features/light/spawn worldgen ring around loaded areas, measured to cover
 roughly the same area as the full chunks themselves) otherwise retain the
 whole per-chunk tree indefinitely: the mapped density-function subtree
 (HolderHolder/Holder.Direct keys in NoiseChunk.wrapped, CubicSpline
 Multipoint/Coordinate, MulOrAdd nodes), the interpolator double[] buffers and
 the aquifer caches; the field is @Nullable and lazily recreated by design so
 clearing is behavior-neutral (a hypothetical later reader rebuilds it
 identically), and per-chunk step sequencing means the write cannot race a
 reader


diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/ChunkAccess.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/ChunkAccess.java
index 54ddcf92e72b9cbd0eb442e5d0faa83c0cf3b33b..0e9f6430bfacc2614e9c9e38c0ef269943293395 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/ChunkAccess.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/ChunkAccess.java
@@ -483,6 +483,22 @@ public abstract class ChunkAccess implements BiomeManager.NoiseBiomeSource, Ligh
         return this.noiseChunk;
     }
 
+    // Papo start - batch 143 (R5): release the per-chunk NoiseChunk once worldgen no longer
+    // reads it. The only readers are the BIOMES/NOISE/SURFACE/CARVERS steps (via
+    // getOrCreateNoiseChunk in NoiseBasedChunkGenerator); chunks parked between carvers and
+    // FULL (features/light/spawn rings around loaded areas) otherwise retain the whole
+    // per-chunk tree for their lifetime: the mapped density-function subtree
+    // (HolderHolder/Holder.Direct keys in NoiseChunk.wrapped, CubicSpline
+    // Multipoint/Coordinate/MulOrAdd nodes), the interpolator double[] buffers and the
+    // aquifer caches - measured scaling with the worldgen ring. The field is @Nullable and
+    // lazily (re)created by design, so clearing it is behavior-neutral: a hypothetical later
+    // reader would just rebuild it identically. Steps are strictly sequenced per chunk by
+    // the chunk system, so this write cannot race a reader of the same chunk.
+    public void papoReleaseNoiseChunk() {
+        this.noiseChunk = null;
+    }
+    // Papo end - batch 143 (R5)
+
     @Deprecated
     public BiomeGenerationSettings carverBiome(Supplier<BiomeGenerationSettings> caverBiomeSettingsSupplier) {
         if (this.carverBiomeSettings == null) {
diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/status/ChunkStatusTasks.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/status/ChunkStatusTasks.java
index d620862e95abf9f098bb53a76825883f2b1f4bbf..da2cf170359beb98a890e9082e9f91ce6c356960 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/status/ChunkStatusTasks.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/status/ChunkStatusTasks.java
@@ -136,6 +136,7 @@ public class ChunkStatusTasks {
                 serverLevel.structureManager().forWorldGenRegion(worldGenRegion),
                 chunk
             );
+        chunk.papoReleaseNoiseChunk(); // Papo - batch 143 (R5): carvers is the last noiseChunk reader
         return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(chunk);
     }
 
